# Raging Battle Mouse ({1}{R}, 2/1): "Celebration — At the beginning of combat on your turn, if two or more nonland permanents
# entered the battlefield under your control this turn, target creature you control gets +1/+1 until end of turn." On turn 1
# Bot1 casts a Black Lotus and, with its mana, the Mouse: exactly two nonland permanents entered (the Lotus counts although it is
# sacrificed, CR 207.2c), so at the beginning of combat the trigger (its only legal target is the Mouse) targets itself and is a 3/2 until end of turn (CR 611.2a).
# At turn 2 (the opponent's turn, no trigger) the Mouse is a 2/1 again (CR 514.2).

